# Patterns catalog (user-agent)

When editing `internal/data/patterns.json` or bot/app/device detectors:

1. Read and apply `.agents/skills/patterns-catalog/SKILL.md`.
2. Prefer `/add-pattern` for the full checklist.

## Local norms

- Every new or changed pattern needs a table-driven test in the owning package.
- Keep patterns specific; avoid substrings that match normal browser UAs
  (e.g. bare `bot` without `heuristic` + `looksLikeBot`).
- Bot matching is case-insensitive `strings.Contains` on the UA; first
  non-heuristic hit wins. Heuristic hits apply only when `looksLikeBot` agrees.
- App patterns with `.*` compile as `(?i)` regexps; others are substring needles.
- Brand keys use token-boundary matching (`prefix` preferred over `pattern`).
  More specific overlapping prefixes must appear before shorter ones.
- Do not add third-party deps for matching; catalog is embedded JSON only.
